\title{PhenotypeTemplates: Generate Phenotype Cohort Definitions from Clinical Context}
\description{
Generates a set of OHDSI cohort definitions for a phenotype from concept sets grouped by clinical role (disease of interest, hypernyms, symptoms, diagnostics, treatments, complications, alternative diagnoses and etiology) and a structured clinical context (clinical course, care setting and expected evidence). Variants are crossed on evidence strictness, index specificity, hospitalization and exclusion of alternative diagnoses, producing a cohort definition set suitable for 'CohortGenerator' and phenotype evaluation.
